<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#piracy">Glossary</a> · Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Piracy</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as pirates</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Piracy is robbery and violence committed at sea. Along the coasts of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> it was a persistent problem, often linked with smuggling and illicit trade. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ming-empire">Ming Empire</a> conducted campaigns against coastal pirates, known in Chinese sources as wokou, as part of its maritime and defensive policy.</p></div>
